## Lifecycle

Xelon creates SOA settings automatically when the DNS zone is created. This resource adopts and manages
that existing zone-owned SOA configuration by calling the backend SOA update endpoint.

The backend has no separate SOA create or delete operation. Destroying `xelon_dns_soa` only removes
the SOA settings from Terraform state. It does not delete, reset, clear, or otherwise modify the remote SOA settings,
and it does not delete the DNS zone managed by `xelon_dns_zone`.

